{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "title: \"Stress Perception — Challenge/Hindrance Appraisal\"\n",
        "format: html\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "## What This Code Does\n",
        "\n",
        "This demo exercises the stress perception phase in isolation. It varies the two appraisal weight parameters — `omega_c` (controllability weight) and `omega_o` (overload weight) — across the full [0, 1] range and observes their effect on challenge, hindrance, appraised stress, and threshold classification.\n",
        "\n",
        "The theory predicts monotonicity: higher `omega_c` produces higher challenge; higher `omega_o` produces higher hindrance. The effective threshold combines both dimensions with opposite signs (`base_threshold + 0.15×challenge − 0.25×hindrance`), making challenge protective and hindrance a vulnerability factor.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Setup"
      ],
      "id": "e4bf2ef3"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| label: setup\n",
        "import os\n",
        "import sys\n",
        "import pathlib\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "import seaborn as sns\n",
        "from numpy.random import Generator, PCG64\n",
        "\n",
        "demos_dir = pathlib.Path(os.getcwd())\n",
        "project_root = demos_dir.parents[2]\n",
        "sys.path.insert(0, str(project_root))\n",
        "\n",
        "from src.python.phases.stress_perception import run_phase"
      ],
      "id": "setup",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Step 1: Sweep Omega_c (Controllability) and Omega_o (Overload)\n",
        "\n",
        "This first sweep runs the perception phase with a fixed mid-range state (controllability=0.5, overload=0.5) and varies both weight parameters. The results record challenge, hindrance, appraised stress, effective threshold, and the binary stress classification."
      ],
      "id": "85c2f82f"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| label: sweep\n",
        "N_C, N_O = 20, 20\n",
        "rng = Generator(PCG64(42))\n",
        "records = []\n",
        "\n",
        "for omega_c in np.linspace(0, 1, N_C):\n",
        "    for omega_o in np.linspace(0, 1, N_O):\n",
        "        state = {\n",
        "            \"stress_controllability\": 0.5, \"stress_overload\": 0.5,\n",
        "            \"volatility\": 0.5, \"recent_stress_intensity\": 0.0,\n",
        "            \"stress_momentum\": 0.0, \"resilience\": 0.5,\n",
        "        }\n",
        "        config = {\n",
        "            \"omega_c\": omega_c, \"omega_o\": omega_o, \"bias\": 0.0,\n",
        "            \"gamma\": 6.0, \"delta\": 0.2, \"base_threshold\": 0.5,\n",
        "            \"challenge_scale\": 0.15, \"hindrance_scale\": 0.25,\n",
        "        }\n",
        "        out = run_phase(state, config, rng)\n",
        "        records.append({\n",
        "            \"omega_c\": omega_c, \"omega_o\": omega_o,\n",
        "            \"challenge\": out[\"observation\"][\"challenge\"],\n",
        "            \"hindrance\": out[\"observation\"][\"hindrance\"],\n",
        "            \"appraised_stress\": out[\"observation\"][\"appraised_stress\"],\n",
        "            \"effective_threshold\": out[\"observation\"][\"effective_threshold\"],\n",
        "            \"is_stressed\": int(out[\"observation\"][\"is_stressed\"]),\n",
        "        })\n",
        "\n",
        "df = pd.DataFrame(records)\n",
        "print(f\"Generated {len(df)} data points ({N_C}×{N_O} sweep)\")"
      ],
      "id": "sweep",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Step 2: Correlogram Analysis\n",
        "\n",
        "The PairGrid below shows all pairwise relationships between the six variables. The diagonal shows density distributions; off-diagonal scatter plots reveal correlations."
      ],
      "id": "be9ed409"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| label: fig-correlogram\n",
        "vars_ = [\"omega_c\", \"omega_o\", \"challenge\", \"hindrance\", \"appraised_stress\", \"effective_threshold\"]\n",
        "g = sns.PairGrid(df[vars_], diag_sharey=False)\n",
        "g.map_upper(sns.scatterplot, s=8, alpha=0.4)\n",
        "g.map_lower(sns.scatterplot, s=8, alpha=0.4)\n",
        "g.map_diag(sns.kdeplot, fill=True)\n",
        "\n",
        "for i, var_i in enumerate(vars_):\n",
        "    for j, var_j in enumerate(vars_):\n",
        "        if i < j:\n",
        "            r_val = df[[var_i, var_j]].corr().iloc[0, 1]\n",
        "            ax = g.axes[i, j]\n",
        "            ax.text(0.95, 0.95, f\"r={r_val:.2f}\", transform=ax.transAxes,\n",
        "                    ha=\"right\", va=\"top\", fontsize=8,\n",
        "                    bbox=dict(boxstyle=\"round,pad=0.2\", facecolor=\"wheat\", alpha=0.7))\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.suptitle(\"Stress Perception — Omega Sweep Correlogram\", y=1.02, fontsize=13)\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "fig-correlogram",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## What We See\n",
        "\n",
        "- **omega_c vs challenge** — monotonic positive correlation (r ≈ 1.0). Higher controllability weight amplifies challenge appraisal.\n",
        "- **omega_o vs hindrance** — likewise monotonic positive (r ≈ 1.0). Higher overload weight amplifies hindrance.\n",
        "- **Complementarity in threshold** — challenge raises the threshold (protective), hindrance lowers it (vulnerability), visible in opposite-sign correlations with `effective_threshold`.\n",
        "- **Classification boundary** — `is_stressed` divides the omega space: the challenge/hindrance balance determines whether `appraised_stress > effective_threshold`.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Why This Matters for the Simulation\n",
        "\n",
        "Stress perception is the gateway to all downstream stress processing. The monotonic relationship between appraisal weights and challenge/hindrance outputs ensures that the perception phase responds predictably to parameter changes. The complementarity of challenge and hindrance in threshold computation implements a core theoretical prediction: protective factors raise the bar for stress classification while vulnerability factors lower it. This directly affects coping outcomes, resource allocation, and ultimately population-level stress dynamics."
      ],
      "id": "ba092d13"
    }
  ],
